 "admissions_overview": {
  "summary": "Admission to Nigerian universities is coordinated by the Joint Admissions and Matriculation Board (JAMB). Candidates sit the Unified Tertiary Matriculation Examination (UTME) and choose institutions and courses on JAMB's system. Universities then run their own screening (Post-UTME) and recommend candidates, and JAMB approves admissions through its Central Admissions Processing System (CAPS), where candidates accept or reject offers. Candidates with qualifications such as HND, NCE, a first degree or A-levels may apply for Direct Entry.",
  "official_url": "https://www.jamb.gov.ng",
  "notes": "Minimum scores, each university's own admittable scores, the UTME timetable, Post-UTME arrangements and available courses change every year. Check jamb.gov.ng and the admissions page of your chosen university each year."
 },
